> It has always seemed to me that if a I was in hand-to-hand combat with
> a foo and the foo was blinded, it would continue hitting me unless I
> moved, at which point it would have to "find" me again. Am I in error
> here? And does blindness/invisibility/displacement work the same in
> this regard? (I.e., are there any situations in which a monster can't
> "see" you but remembers where you are?)

     If you're invisible or displaced and the monster doesn't already
know where you are, it will guess.  (The guess is less likely to find
you for displacement than it is for invisibility.)  However, once it
does find you by guessing, it will remember that spot.  If you haven't
moved by the next time it tries to attack, it won't need to guess and
will just hit you.

     I don't recall offhand whether a blinded monster behaves similarly
to you being invisible and am too lazy to look it up at the moment.


